// ---- Patch notes (newest first). Every update to the game adds an entry here and bumps SQ_VERSION. ----
const PATCH_NOTES=[
 {v:'2026.11.26-1',d:'Nov 26, 2026',t:"Buffs that last through a refresh, saves behind screens and bug fixes",n:["Potion, meal and shrine buffs now last through a refresh or logging out: the time left is saved, and it waits for you while you're away.","PvP ON is now a small red chip in the row under your quest, so it never covers the quest you're doing.","Caves without a boss now say so when you enter them.","Fixed: progress made while a screen or the menu was open (fishing, brewing, cooking and smithing go on behind screens) could miss the save to your account, so switching devices soon after could take you back. The game now keeps saving behind screens.","Fixed: a new character made on a device that had been used for another account started with that account's pets, capes and dyes.","Fixed: a fishing rod that wore out kept catching fish. Fishing now stops when the worn-out rod comes off.","Fixed: while cooking at a stove (or smelting or forging) in a house, the bag showed everything in your chests too and jumped around. It shows only your bag now.","Fixed: the stove said only \"Cooked 1.\" for every piece. It now says what you cooked: \"Cooked 1 trout.\"","Fixed: brewing messages jumped to the message box every few brews (when you kept ingredients or made a double batch) instead of showing by your character.","Fixed: repairs say when a bar breaks into shards and how many shards are left in your bag (10 shards fuse back into a bar at a furnace).","Fixed: the Hunter perk's +2 against wolves showed as a separate number; it's now part of the arrow's damage.","Fixed: the last seeds of the day at the General Store couldn't be bought (pumpkin seeds come 3 to a pack, so the last 2 were stuck). The last pack now sells what's left for that share of the price.","Fixed: starving no longer wears down your armour (only hits you take do).","Fixed: your health could show long decimals (like 4.333333/6). It shows one decimal at most.","Fixed: other players inside a house, shop or cave on an island showed on the map as if they were on Hollow. They now show on their island, at the door they went in by.","Fixed: chopping on Shattered Expanse announced logs and wood that never reached your bag. Every \"+N logs\" message now matches what you get.","Fixed: the newest pets (like the pupper) couldn't be placed in your home. Now they can."]},
 {v:'2026.11.25-5',d:'Nov 25, 2026',t:"New HUD colours and total level next to every name",n:["The HUD has a new look, like an old scroll instead of the old blue and white: parchment-tan boxes with a soft gradient and a faint grain, carved brown edges with little corner studs, and dark-brown text. Messages unroll between scroll ends, and the HP, FOOD and MANA bars sit in grooves in softer colours. Your status box, quest tracker, minimap, START menu, buttons and screens all match.","Everyone's total level now shows next to their name. Over their head you'll see their name and their total level in gold, like Jace [987], and your own HP and FOOD box shows yours after your name (Lv.987). A player's level appears over their head once they've updated their game.","Fixed: on phones, sliding your finger off the HIT button while your other thumb was moving caused an error in the background."]},
 {v:'2026.11.24-14',d:'Nov 24, 2026',t:"Smithing XP from materials, new Woodcutting, longer-lasting upgrades and a new wiki",n:["Smithing now works out the XP and the time of every furnace and anvil recipe from what goes into it. Every bar, ore, log, gem and other material has its own XP and time, and a recipe gives the XP and takes the time of all its materials added up. Bigger gear takes longer and gives more: an adamant chestplate (4 adamant bars) takes twice as long as an adamant sword (2 bars) and gives twice the XP.","Each furnace and anvil recipe shows how long it takes at your level and how much XP it gives, like 1.4 s · 340 xp.","What changed: most iron, steel, mithril and adamant recipes give about the same XP as before. Meteorite bars and meteorite gear give a lot more (a meteorite chestplate went from 2,000 to 6,000 XP), the starsteel dagger and bows give more, and arrows give about half as much. Small things like arrows and iron daggers are quicker to make, and a meteorite bar takes much longer to smelt. Repairs and upgrades follow the new XP.","Woodcutting has a new rhythm. Every chop takes 1 second at Woodcutting 1 and 0.0025 seconds less for every level (0.75 seconds at 99), every axe has a chopping power (wooden 1, stone 1.25, iron 1.5, steel 1.75, mithril 2.25, adamant 2.5, meteorite 3) and every tree a toughness (tree and pine 2, oak 5, willow 10, maple 17, yew 24, void 39), so higher trees take longer and a better axe always helps. A yew takes 10 chops with an adamant axe, about 8.5 seconds at Woodcutting 60.","Trees now pay as they go down: each quarter of a tree gives 1 log and a quarter of its XP, and when it falls you get 1 log up to your extra log limit, so every tree is a bit of a dice roll. Your limit starts at 1. Oak, willow, maple and yew trees give only their own logs (no plain wood on top).","New Woodcutting perks: every 10 levels, choose Quick Chop (every chop takes 0.05 seconds less: with all nine, a chop takes about 0.3 seconds at level 99) or Bigger Haul (+1 extra log limit, up to 10 with all nine). Quick Chop levels you fastest; Bigger Haul gets you more logs. They replace the old Woodcutting perks and the old speed-ups and extra-log chances. If you had Woodcutting perks, pick them again in Skills: it's free this time.","Axe upgrades now give +1, +2 or +3 extra log limit instead of faster chops. Rare Heartwood can still turn up when a tree falls, and treeling pets can shake loose an extra log with every payout.","Void trees now need Woodcutting 75 and an adamant axe or better, on the Shattered Expanse and on guild islands, and give 400 Woodcutting XP each.","The Void Treant now takes 10,000 void logs to summon (20,000 to keep your Woodcutting rank) instead of 50,000, since void trees take longer to chop.","The wiki (START > Wiki) has a new look and a new layout. Its pages are grouped into sections down the left side (Getting started, Skills, Items, Making things, Monsters, World, Quests, Together and What's new), and every page says what it covers at the top. On phones the sections sit in a row along the top.","The wiki's Home page is new: your next steps, the skills that unlock something soon (with a bar for how close you are), what you unlocked lately, skills you haven't tried yet, the latest update and buttons into every section. New players also get a short guide to the basics.","Wiki > Items is split into groups (weapons, armour, tools, food, ores and bars, logs, fish and more) and no longer lists the +1, +2, +3 and worn copies of every item. Search still finds everything.","Gear pages in the wiki now show a card with the item's slot, stats, what it needs, how long it lasts before it wears out and what its upgrades do. Axe pages show their chopping power and how long each tree takes.","Wiki > Skills shows how long each thing takes and links every item. Woodcutting lists every tree, void trees included, and about how long each one takes to fell with the axe you'd have by then.","New wiki pages: Controls (under Getting started) and guides to gear wearing out, upgrading gear, trees and axes, and smithing XP and time.","Upgraded gear lasts much longer: a +1 lasts 10 times as long as the plain item, a +2 100 times, and a +3 never wears out. Used upgraded gear you already have keeps the share of durability it had (a +1 at 25% is still at 25%, of a much bigger number), and used +3s become plain +3s.","The game now tells you what level each upgrade needs. Every item you can upgrade lists it at the end of its description (for example, an adamant sword: +1 at Smithing 75, +2 at 85, +3 at 95), an upgraded item says what the next level needs, the equipment screen shows it for the piece you're wearing, and the Blacksmith's bench lists the level on every upgrade, not only the ones you can't make yet.","Wiki > Skills > Fishing now lists every fish: all 16, including the island fish, the moonfin, the abyssal eel, the ancient koi and the rainbow fish, with the Fishing level each needs, where it bites, the Cooking level to cook it and how much it heals. It also says how to get a rod and what bait does. The Fishing tree in the Skills screen now names the island fish too.","When a tree falls, the message now says where your extra log limit comes from, for example \"(felled: 2 of 1-2: +1 from your +1 axe)\".","Fixed: the wiki's axe descriptions still said how much an axe \"hits for\" from before trees changed today, and a few other descriptions (the furnace, anvil, iron ore, iron bars and boss cores) were out of date.","Fixed: since this morning's wiki update, the wiki couldn't be scrolled on phones held upright. It scrolls again.","Fixed: with the sledgehammer in your hand, chopping trees and mining rocks showed the sledgehammer swing instead of your axe or pickaxe. Now trees always show the axe and rocks the pickaxe (the sledgehammer still smashes small rocks in one hit, and boulders still show the sledgehammer). Your axe also stays in your hands for the whole chop instead of your weapon swinging at the end.","Fixed: facing left, your axe, pickaxe, sword and wand were held backwards (an axe's blade faced away from the tree). Facing left is now the mirror image of facing right.","Fixed: other players couldn't see you chopping trees or mining rocks. Now they see your axe or pickaxe swing in your hands, and hear it when they're close.","Fixed: trees, rocks and bushes on guild islands weren't shared between members, so a tree you chopped down was still standing for everyone else. Now they're shared like on every other island: once one member uses something up, it's gone for everyone until it grows back 60 seconds later.","Fixed: right after a chop you walked slowly for as long as the chop took (up to a second), so walking away from a fallen tree felt sluggish. Now a chop slows you for only a quarter of a second, like a sword swing. Your next chop still waits for the whole chop time.","Fixed: after another player reloaded the game (for example to get an update), you stopped seeing their sword swings, arrows, spells, ultimates and chops until you reloaded too. Now you see them right away."]},
 {v:'2026.11.23-11',d:'Nov 23, 2026',t:"The Blacksmith's bench: repairs, upgrades and cores, sunken treasure and fixes",n:["Gear now wears out as you use it. Swords and daggers wear a little with every hit that lands, bows and wands with every shot, each armour piece with every hit you take, and axes, pickaxes and fishing rods with every log, ore or fish. The hoe and watering can never wear out. Better gear lasts longer: wooden tools 250 uses, stone tools and bought gear 500, iron 1,000, steel 1,500, mithril 2,500, adamant 4,000, boss gear 5,000 and meteorite 6,000, and 10% more for each upgrade level. Bows last twice as many shots and wands 1.5 times as many casts, armour loses 5 points for every hit you take, and the fishing rod lasts 2,000 catches.","Only the piece you're wearing wears down: spare copies stay brand new. Take a used piece off and it shows in your bag with what's left, like Used adamant sword (62%), and keeps that number in chests and trades. The equipment screen shows a durability bar on every slot.","You get a warning at 20%. At 0 the piece comes off into your bag as a greyed-out Worn-out copy, separate from your new ones. It isn't destroyed, but you can't wear it again until it's repaired.","Repair your gear at the Blacksmith's bench, at the level that makes the item plus 5 (Smithing or Crafting). A full repair costs half of the item's main material and gives half its crafting XP; a smaller repair costs and gives less. Bars split into 10 shards for small repairs, and spare shards fuse back into a bar at a furnace. Boss gear takes 10 sigil shards from its island. Bought gear (the leather set, the wizard set and shop wands) can't be repaired: buy a new one.","Can't repair something yourself? Trade it to a smith: they repair it at their bench and trade it back. Used gear can't be sold until it's repaired, and it stays with you when you fall like the rest of your gear.","Fishing rods can always be crafted now (Craft > Tools, Crafting 3: 4 wood and 1 iron ore). If you already have one, the new rod goes in your bag as a spare for when yours wears out.","Upgrade your gear at the Blacksmith's bench, up to +3. 10 of the same item make a +1, 10 of the +1 make a +2, and 10 of the +2 make a +3. The piece you're wearing counts toward the 10. You need the level that makes the item plus 10 for a +1 (plus 20 for a +2, plus 30 for a +3), in the skill that makes it, and you get a big chunk of XP. Boss gear like the Warlord's blade, the Flame crown or the Spider set takes cores from its island instead: 1 core for a +1, 10 for a +2, 100 for a +3, at level 70, 80 and 90.","What each level gives: swords, bows and wands hit 5% harder, axes and pickaxes chop and mine 5% faster, each armour piece blocks 1% more and raises your block limit by 1%, ranger pieces also make your arrows fly 5% further, and daggers do 1 more damage at +2 and 2 more at +3. Upgrades don't count in PvP. Upgraded items show their level on their icon and name, and you can trade and sell them.","New furniture: the Blacksmith's bench (Craft > Building, Crafting 12: 3 iron bars, 4 stone, 10 wood). Place it at home and smith cores from sigil shards: 100 shards from one island make one core and give 1,000 Smithing XP. Briar cores need Smithing 40, Ember 50, Frost and Silver 60, Void 70. Boss gear is upgraded with them. The bench uses the shards in your house's chests too.","Arrows and bows are now made at an anvil and train Smithing instead of Archery, at the same levels and for the same XP. The shortbow and longbow go into your bag like other bows; equip them from there. The ranger hood, chaps and vest are now made in the Craft menu (and at a crafting bench) with Crafting, at the same levels. Archery now trains by shooting.","Iron axes and pickaxes now come only from an anvil (Smithing 5, 2 iron bars and 1 wood). The Craft menu no longer makes them from ore.","Fishing: every so often you'll reel in a sunken treasure chest instead of a fish. It opens on the spot: gold (more at higher Fishing levels) and a find or two, like gold bars, healing potions, arrows or even a gem. Sailors say something stranger lies at the bottom of the sea...","Art Room: an Opacity slider for the colour you're using. Lower it to make that colour see-through, for ghosts, glass, water or glowing things. The checkered squares behind a colour show how see-through it is, and see-through colours stay see-through when your art is in the game.","Fixed: on islands you share with other players, like the Shattered Expanse, a reef crawler could end up hidden right under you and keep hurting you while nobody could see it. Other players' monsters now stay where they really are.","Fixed: tapping SLAM (or ULT) while it's recharging now tells you how long is left, instead of saying it didn't start.","Fixed: the anvil showed some materials by their code names (like \"2 abar\" or \"2 maplelog\"). It now says adamant bar, maple logs and so on.","Fixed: the Mushroom Hat now gives 300 Crafting XP like the rest of the mushroom set, the Mushroom Robe needs 45 cotton instead of 1, and the Ancient Helmet gives 900 Smithing XP.","Fixed: swapping an upgraded piece for another one while you had plain copies of it in your bag turned one of the plain copies into an upgraded one.","Fixed: upgraded copies in your bag went into your grave when you fell. They're gear, so they stay with you now.","Fixed: hitting a tree in your backyard from the very edge of your reach did nothing and caused an error.","Fixed: after you closed the World Market with ✕, tapping items in your bag, equipping and the player screen did nothing until you logged in again.","Fixed: on iPhone, a chest's item card could run off the bottom of the screen when you tapped an item lower down in your bag, hiding its buttons.","Fixed: the Smithing perks that give metal back (Metal Saver, Metal Fortune, Precious Metal, and the ones that use fewer bars) now work with mithril, adamant and meteorite bars. Before, they only knew iron and steel bars, so on higher recipes they could save a gem or a log instead, or nothing at all.","Fixed: a dagger in your off-hand could vanish when you loaded the game if your save also had a bow, wand, hoe or watering can in that hand. The dagger now goes in your bag instead."]},
 {v:'2026.11.22-12',d:'Nov 22, 2026',t:"Home tax, Art Room tools, pet cards in Drop Card, chat filter and fixes",n:["Homes now pay a little tax at the bank. Penny the Banker has a stall in Hollow Village, next to the World Market. A house costs 50,000 gold a month (30 days) and a castle 150,000. Every home gets its first 30 days free, starting today for the homes already built. Homes on your guild's island pay half: 25,000 gold a month for a house and 75,000 for a castle. Talk to Penny to pay a month at a time, up to three months ahead. Your bag and your map show how long your tax is paid for, and you get a reminder a week before it runs out.","If a home's tax runs out, the bank takes it off the map and looks after it, with everything inside. Nothing is lost. Pay Penny one month of tax plus 10% to get it back where it stood, with no tax added for the time the bank had it. If someone has built on that spot by then, your home goes into your bag with everything that was in it. You can't place a new home while the bank has yours.","Packing up your home (HIT its walls) pauses its tax. The time you've paid for carries over to the next home you place. If the new home costs a different amount (a castle instead of a house, or a home on or off your guild's island), your paid days change to match, so the gold you paid is worth the same.","Other players stop seeing a home once its tax has run out, so homes nobody looks after don't stay on the map forever.","Guild bosses can now also be summoned without spending a guild skill rank: pay twice the materials instead (100,000 void logs for the Void Treant, 10,000 raw fish for the Giant Turtle). The leader or an officer finds the new button under START > Guild > Bosses.","Art Room (patrons): a new Select tool. Drag a box around part of your drawing (or pick Free and draw any shape around it), then drag inside it to move those pixels somewhere else. The arrow keys nudge it one pixel at a time. Crop cuts the canvas down to what you selected, Delete clears it, and Undo brings anything back.","Art Room: the mouse wheel zooms in and out around the pointer, so the spot you're looking at stays under it.","Art Room: bigger canvases, up to 96 x 96 pixels. A 96 x 96 drawing can have up to 6 frames, smaller ones up to 8.","Art Room: Drafts. Keep several drawings going at once and switch between them: press Drafts to save the one you're on, save a copy, start a new drawing or open an old one. The drawing you're working on saves to its draft as you go. Drafts are kept on the device you drew them on.","Drop Card: pet cards now go in your deck like any other card, and you can bring several (up to 2 of each). When you draw one, pay its cost (1 to 4 Mana) to summon it beside your hero. Up to 3 pets can be out at once, and they don't take any of your 6 monster spots. Pets have ATK and HP: they can attack from your next turn, and they can be attacked and hit by spells. A pet's power works while it's out, and two pets with the same power add up. If a deck had a Companion, that pet card is now in the deck.","Drop Card: you can see the other player's pets beside their hero. Tap any pet (yours or theirs) to see its cost, ATK, HP and power.","Drop Card: drag your cards. Drag a card from your hand onto the table to play it, or drag a spell onto its target. Drag one of your monsters or pets onto an enemy, or onto the enemy hero, to attack. Tapping works too.","Ace now brings a pet to Drop Card matches: a Dog on Normal, and a Wolf and an Imp on Hard.","The cooking stove has a Cook everything button: it cooks all your raw food, every kind, one after another, from your bag and the chests nearby. Food your Cooking level can't cook yet is left alone.","The HERE map now shows where everyone on your island is: a blue dot with the player's name (green for friends). Party members are still shown in green.","Fixed: in Drop Card, wolf powers never worked. The Frostfang Alpha gives your other wolves +1 ATK, and the Wolf pet cards boost your wolves.","Fixed: in Drop Card, the Mithril golem's power (your Guard monsters get +2 HP) now also works on monsters that got Guard from an Iron skin potion, whether you use the potion before or after summoning the golem.","Fixed: the chat filter starred ordinary words and numbers, like \"as\", amounts such as 45, 455 or 1000000, and two normal words that happened to spell something together (\"this hit\"). It leaves those alone now, and \"hoe\" is allowed (it's a farming tool). Swear words are still caught, even split up or spelled with numbers.","Fixed: on a computer, the SLAM (or ULT) box under your quest list looked like a button but did nothing when clicked, and nothing said how to use it. Your ultimate is the V key (or the key you picked in Options > Controls), and the box now says so, for example \"SLAM (V)\". It turns purple when your ultimate is ready, and clicking it uses it too.","Fixed: house icons on the map were too big and covered the towns around them. They're half the size now.","Fixed: on some phones, tapping the SLAM (or ULT) button could do nothing. The button now reacts to the very first touch, still works if something invisible is lying over it, and if your ultimate can't start it tells you why and sends us a report so we can fix the cause.","Fixed: restarting the game cut every Drop Card deck down to 2 tree cards, so the Starter Deck came back with 16 cards and couldn't be played. Decks keep all their cards now, and a Starter Deck that lost its Trees gets them back.","Adults can now turn the chat filter off: Options > Chat filter. With it off, you see other adults' messages exactly as they typed them. Messages from younger players are always filtered, emails, phone numbers and links are always hidden, and everyone else still sees your messages filtered.","Fixed: in the Art Room, pressing any button while zoomed in jumped the view back to the top left corner. It stays where you were now.","Fixed: on some phone browsers (like Brave), guild sails looked speckled. They show your guild's colours properly now.","Fixed: when the World Market couldn't take an offer (for example, when all your offer slots were in use), phones didn't show why, so a purchase could look like it went through. The reason now shows on the market screen, under the price.","Fixed: packing up a house with a framed card in it lost the card. Cards in frames now go back to your Card Binder when their home is packed up, and cards lost this way earlier have come back too.","Fixed: seen from behind, a cape covered long hair. Long hair now hangs down over your cape.","Fixed: visitors to your house (or island home) saw an empty stand on your card frames. They see the card you put up now."]},
 {v:'2026.11.21-21',d:'Nov 21, 2026',t:"Drop Card against other players, new tree cards and fixes",n:["Mana now stops refilling for 1.5 seconds after you cast a spell or use an ultimate. Keep casting and your mana runs down; stop for a moment and it refills as fast as before. (Before this, mages in mage armour got mana back faster than they could spend it.)","On phones and tablets, hold the CAST or BOW button to keep firing at the nearest enemy, the same way holding HIT keeps swinging. A quick tap still fires once, and you can still drag the button to aim.","Fixed: the World Market refused some items with long names, like Spider Weaver Robes (\"The market couldn't take that offer\"). They can be bought and sold now, and offers also go up on phones whose clock is running fast.","Fixed: with a screen open (your bag, skills or a shop), fishing and Make all kept going without using any food, so you could skill forever. Skilling behind a screen now uses food like normal and stops when you run out. You still don't get hungry inside your house or castle, or next to your own campfire with Hearthkeeper.","Fixed: the \"N left\" count over your head disappeared when smithing with materials from nearby chests.","Fixed: the campfire list promised burn times over 30 minutes. A campfire burns for 30 minutes at most, and the list now shows the time you'll actually get.","Fixed: Ace's card table from Hollow Village also showed up on the islands (on top of a tree in Briarwood).","Fixed: brewing a double batch now gives XP for both potions, and the message tells you when you kept some of your ingredients.","Fixed: a second Drop Card match against the same player ended after the first turn (one of you saw a draw, the other that the player left). Rematches now play out. You both need this update to play each other.","Fixed: on islands with other players (most often the Shattered Expanse), you could keep losing health every second or so with nothing around you, and the only way to stop it was to leave the island. It happened when another player's connection dropped for a moment. It can't happen any more.","Fixed: DEPOSIT BAG on a chest also put all your Drop Cards into the chest, so they disappeared from your Card Binder. It leaves your cards alone now. If cards went missing, look in the chests you deposited into and take them back.","Fixed: pet cards had names like \"pweb\" and \"psquir\". They now have proper names (Pet Card: Webling, Pet Card: Squirrel...), and every pet's card shows in your Card Binder and in the wiki, not just the ones you have.","BURN FIRST for logs: select a log in your bag and tap ☆ BURN FIRST. FIRE then builds your campfire with that log (or feeds it to the fire you're standing at) without asking.","Hearthkeeper now needs a real campfire: standing near a castle outside no longer keeps you from getting hungry. Inside houses and castles you still don't get hungry.","Fixed: building a campfire from oak or better logs gave back plain wood when a Firemaking perk saved fuel. You now get back the log you burned.","Fixed: an oak (or better) campfire showed two separate XP numbers. It now shows one total.","Fixed: Meteor Fall (the meteorite wand's ultimate) didn't get the cooldown cuts from Magic levels and Ultimate Focus.","Fixed: when you switched to another tab or minimised the game, it kept running without showing anything, so you could come back starved or fallen. Your skilling still carries on in the background and you still get hungry, but you can't get hurt, and if your food runs out whatever you were doing stops.","Fixed: while you played Drop Card, the game kept going behind the table, so you could starve or be attacked by monsters you couldn't see. You're now safe at the card table: you can't lose health and you don't get hungry.","Cook all for meals: stoves now have a Cook all button for meals like pizza and stew.","Castle and house yards: with your hoe out, press HIT twice on tilled soil to fill it back in (a crop growing there comes back as its seed).","Fixed: the gold amulet's +5% XP and the emerald ring's +10% gathering XP weren't being added. They work again and are listed under your stats.","Fixed: forging armour at the anvil put it straight on you. It now goes into your bag so you can equip it when you want.","Fixed: Smith all and Smelt all counted down to \"0 left\" and kept going when you got materials back. The count now includes them.","Fixed: the Outlaw Country quests told you to return to Mira in No Man's Land. The tracker now points you to her in Dusthaven.","Fixed: a dodge roll could carry you into a wall and get you stuck.","Your Card Binder is now the CARDS tab in your bag instead of an item, so it can't be lost, and your Drop Cards stay with you when you fall instead of going into your grave.","Drop Card rule changes: heroes now start with 30 HP (was 20), decks can be anywhere from 20 to 60 cards (was exactly 20), and your Grove holds up to 6 trees instead of 10 Mana, so bigger trees like Yews and Void trees give you more Mana to work with.","Play Drop Card against other players! Stand next to someone, tap their name and choose PLAY DROP CARD. Like chess, you can both stake items or gold, and the winner takes both stakes. You each play the deck that's active in your Card Binder, at the same card table as Ace's matches. You have 2 minutes a turn (your turn ends by itself after that). Giving up, leaving or going offline loses the match. Win one for the Card duelist achievement.","New Drop Cards: Pine (1 Mana), Dead tree (1 Mana) and Void tree (6 Mana). Chop pines, the dead trees of Ashfall and the void trees of the Shattered Expanse for a chance at their card.","Fixed: a copy of the game left open from before Drop Cards could wipe your cards when you tapped PLAY HERE INSTEAD after playing on another device. PLAY HERE INSTEAD now reloads the game first, and old copies of the game can no longer save over your account.","Fixed: finding a pet you already have (an imp from a world boss, or a pet on an island) turned it away. The extra one now goes into your bag, so you can keep it, sell it, trade it or release it for its Drop Card.","Fixed: playing on a device with an older copy of the game could wipe your Drop Cards and Card Binder from your account. The game now keeps every item in your save, even ones it doesn't know yet.","Fixed: Drop Card matches against players said your deck wasn't allowed when your Companion was a pet card the other player's game didn't know about, or when your deck had more than 20 of one tree. If the two games ever disagree about a match, it now stops as a draw and gives the stakes back.","Fixed: a Drop Card match against a player whose game was out of date ended as soon as it started. Now the game tells you before any stakes are taken, and you both need to close and reopen the game.","Fixed: every tree now gives its own card. Yews, pines and dead trees could give the plain Tree card, and void trees gave no card at all.","Fixed: cacti give the Cactus fruit card instead of a Tree card.","Shiny cards can be seen in your Card Binder: the new ★ Shiny filter shows every shiny card you own, and a card you have both ways shows its normal and shiny pictures side by side when you tap it.","Fixed: after looking at another player's cards, your own Card Binder showed their cards until you restarted the game."]},
 {v:'2026.11.20-20',d:'Nov 20, 2026',t:"Guild raids, Outlaw Country, Merchant skill and a GE-style market",n:["Play Drop Card! Talk to Ace the Card Sharp in Hollow Village and play your deck against him on Easy, Normal or Hard. Plant a tree each turn, chop trees to pay for cards (stumps grow back next turn), play monsters and spells, and attack Ace's monsters or Ace himself. Boss cards have their own powers and your pet card is your Companion. Win for gold (50 / 150 / 400, a tenth after your first win of the day at that level) and the Card shark achievement. The match is played at a wooden card table with you and Ace at either end, your Groves of real trees, and your hand fanned out. Tap any card (in your hand, on the table, a tree or your pet) to see it up close with its stats, power and where it's found, and to play, plant, chop or attack from there; tap anywhere else to go back to the table. Works with touch, mouse and controller (○ or Esc goes back).","Drop Cards are here: every monster, tree and boss now has its own collectible card. Each monster has a 1% chance to drop its card when you beat it, each tree a 1% chance when you chop it (better trees give more Mana), and every world, dungeon, island and guild boss has a 1% chance to drop its own rare card. Your cards live in a Card Binder (one bag slot): tap it and OPEN to see your collection and build up to 3 decks. Potions you brew and berries, mushrooms, nuts and cactus fruit you forage can drop cards too, and releasing a pet now always gives you its Pet Card. Learn everything in Drop Card for Dummies, 1 gold at the General Store in Hollow Village: your first copy comes with a free 20-card Starter Deck. And if you go a long time without a card, the next one is guaranteed. The Drop Card game itself is coming soon.","Every card you find flips onto your screen, and about 1 in 50 is a SHINY card in inverted colours (it plays the same as the normal one). Boss cards and shiny cards are announced in chat for everyone online. New Drop Card achievements reward collecting.","Meet Ace the Card Sharp at his card table next to the chess table in Hollow Village: he sells Drop Card for Dummies, explains the game and opens your binder. Tap DROP CARDS in another player's menu to see their collection, and check the new Drop Cards leaderboard.","Card frames: craft one at the workbench (4 wood + 1 iron bar) or buy one at Marlo's Emporium, place it in your house and press HIT on it to put one of your cards on display.","Pick your mouse cursor in Options > Cursor: gold arrow, sword, wand, gauntlet, high contrast, a yellow crosshair, an inverted crosshair that takes the opposite colour of whatever's under it, or whatever's in your off-hand. Each comes in Normal or Large. With a controller, the right stick now moves a cursor around menus and screens, and \u2715 clicks with it (out in the world it still aims).","Keep a friend's campfire going: stand next to anyone's fire and press F (or the fire button) to feed it a log. Once you've fed it, it keeps burning even after the player who lit it logs out.","Discord roles: link your Discord account in Options > Link Discord, post the code in #link on the SkillQuest Discord, and the SQ Bot gives you roles for your Total Level, your guild, Patron, and game Moderator or Developer, plus a private channel for your guild that only its members can see. They update by themselves as you play.","Chat messages can be twice as long: up to 160 characters in public chat, private messages, party chat and guild chat. Speech bubbles show up to 5 lines.","Fixed: monsters drawn off the screen could still bite you (\"Ouch!\" with nothing around you). Only a monster you can actually see can touch you now, and if you fall to one you couldn't see, the game sends us a report by itself so we can track down where it came from.","Fixed: with a Stone Sledgehammer and the Dragonsoul amulet both worn, the ULT button said SLAM even when Dragon Form was the ultimate picked in your gear tab (and turned you into a dragon). The button now shows the ultimate it will use.","The arrow count by your HP bar shows the arrows your bow will shoot next (it always shoots your best ones first), with their picture.","Fixed: Patron paintings saved on your device didn't load before your save, and pets' item finds and powers used your position instead of the pet's.","The Void Treant and the Giant Turtle are real guild raids now: three times the health, faster attacks, and a second rage at a quarter health. The Treant's shockwave throws you back and can't be rolled through, it burrows and bursts up somewhere else, void poison washes over the whole arena, it sometimes glows green and HEALS from every hit (stop attacking!), and void saplings hunt one fighter each (they can't be hurt and switch targets every 8 seconds). The Turtle's tidal waves throw you back, its whirlpools pull you in, and it spins around in its shell where it can't be hurt. START > Guild > Bosses shows this week's top 5 damage.","Outlaw Country: Mira at Dusthaven's Oasis Rest has a new quest line that takes you into No Man's Land, where PvP is always on: scout the badlands, collect bandit bounties, carry her satchel to Dustwater (fall and you lose it), mine the hills, beat two players there, and take down Black Jack, the Outlaw King. Big gold and XP rewards.","Mines need Mining levels: the Old Ironcrest Mine needs Mining 30 and Deepvein Mine Mining 45 to go in, and every two floors down need 10 more (mines on other islands start at 15). Mines now have about twice the monsters, a little tougher, to match all that ore.","Guild Quests grow: each quest your guild finishes in a skill doubles the next one in that skill (100,000 trees, then 200,000, then 400,000...). Quests already running keep their goal.","New skill: Merchant. Every sale you make on the World Market gives Merchant XP, and every 20 Merchant levels gives you one more market offer slot (up to 12).","The World Market works more like the Grand Exchange: My offers shows your offer slots as boxes with progress bars (and Buy / Sell buttons in the empty ones), and Browse, Buy and Sell have a search box and categories (ores and bars, logs, fish and food, gear, potions, gems and jewelry, farming) with items in a grid.","Gluttony: reach Cooking 99 and you eat on your own when you're down to half health (turn it off in Options).","Bonus items give XP: an extra or doubled log, ore, fish or crop from your perks, and a bonus item when smithing, crafting or cooking, now give the XP that item would have.","The game keeps going when you switch to another tab or minimise it on a computer, so a make-all, fishing or a fire carries on.","Town names: the town you're in is shown on the minimap, and a wooden sign with its name slides down when you walk in.","Magic balance: mana comes back more slowly at low Magic levels (normal speed at Magic 1, three times as fast from Magic 25, as before). Mana Shield is now Mana Barrier: it absorbs one blow every 30 seconds, not every blow.","Item descriptions no longer claim to be the best in the game (that stopped being true as new gear came out). They say what they beat instead.","Fixed: harbor posts on islands (guild islands too) didn't respond, so you couldn't sail home. Island folk, guild boards, the guild bank and loot chests on islands answer again too.","Hold HIT on a phone or tablet to keep swinging, like holding Space or R2: keep your finger on the button to keep chopping, mining or fighting.","The wiki says where meteorite ore and stardust come from: meteor strikes (the banner tells you where one has fallen).","Fixed: monsters could hide under island houses and castles (on the door or behind the roof) and hurt anyone walking past without being seen. They're moved out from under buildings now, and one that's still hidden can't touch you.","Fixed: visitors to a castle on an island only saw the back half of its furniture, and could walk through the walls built inside it. They see the whole hall now.","Fixed: Guild Quests started before the new doubling goals stopped counting progress. They count again.","Fixed: in PvP, your hardest hits (ultimates and strong weapons, 3 hearts) were refused by the server with an \"online server refused that\" message and never landed. They land now.","Fixed: pressing Link Discord again made a new code and the one you'd already posted in #link stopped working. You keep the same code all day now.","Fixed: if you fell while in Dragon Form with a screen open, you could get up still in Dragon Form.","Fixed: with a controller plugged in, its gold highlight stayed on whatever the controller last pointed at while you clicked with the mouse, so clicks in the bag, gear tab and skills looked like they did nothing. Clicking or tapping now switches to mouse mode (the highlight goes away), and touching the controller switches back."]},
 {v:'2026.11.19-2',d:'Nov 19, 2026',t:"The Song Studio, new pets, song zones and a better wiki",n:["The wiki has a page for every item and monster: tap any name to see how to get it (recipes, shops, which monsters drop it and how often, where to gather it) and what it's used for. ◀ Back takes you where you were.","New wiki tabs: Brewing, Playing together (parties, trading, the market, duels, chess), Patrons and Achievements (with your progress). Home shows what you unlocked lately and skills you haven't tried yet, and search finds item and monster pages.","Patrons: the Song Studio is open (START > Patron > Song Studio). Pick a mood, tap notes on a grid and send your song in. No music experience needed: the grid only has notes that fit the song, the bright rows go with every chord, and \"Make me a tune\" and \"Pick chords for me\" give you a start. Approved songs can play in the game, with your name in the credits.","New pets can now come to the game, including pets Patrons draw in the Art Room.","Places on an island can now have music of their own, so a different song can play as you walk into them.","The HERE map now lists the players online under it, like the WORLD map, and marks the ones on your island."]},
 {v:'2026.11.18-5',d:'Nov 18, 2026',t:"Bug fixes, fishing behind menus and colourful campfires",n:["Campfires show what they're made of: oak burns golden, willow blue, maple crimson, yew green and void logs purple, and each one glows in its own colour at night. The kindling you're lighting shows the log's colour too.","You can eat while cooking at a fire: press EAT while your food cooks and you eat something without stopping the cooking.","Fixed: fishing stopped while a menu or screen was open. Bites now keep coming and the line reels in behind the menu.","Fixed: with a full bag, a chest's item card could be cut off at the bottom of the screen on iPhone, hiding its buttons. It now always fits on screen.","Fixed: on Ironcrest (and anywhere else a path meets a rocky plateau), you couldn't step from the path onto the plateau's side even though nothing was in the way. Paths now lead straight onto plateaus from the north, east and west. The cliff faces on the south side still need the stone stairs.","Fixed: since earlier today, HIT could do two things at once: reeling in a fish or placing something also swung your weapon, and other buttons that take over HIT did the same. HIT does one thing again.","Fixed: smelting, smithing or crafting at a station in your house (or next to chests outdoors) could save your game with the chests' contents counted in your bag as well. If you closed the game soon after, the next time it loaded those items were in both places. Saves now never count items borrowed from chests.","Fixed: getting up very quickly after falling could lose everything you carried without leaving a gravestone. Your things now always go into your grave, or stay in your bag if there's nowhere to put one.","Fixed: closing the game while lighting a campfire with oak or better logs could turn those logs into plain wood.","Fixed: on phones, the world boss bar covered the getting-started tips. It now sits below them."]},
 {v:'2026.11.17-3',d:'Nov 17, 2026',t:"Market prices set by players, better character screen",n:["Every item now has a market price worked out from what players actually paid for it on the World Market: the middle price of the last 30 days' sales. You'll see it when you buy or sell (with a little chart of recent sales), in your bag and on chest item cards. Items nobody has traded lately just show the shop price.","Sales on the World Market of 100 gold or more now pay a 1% market tax, taken from the seller's gold. It keeps gold from piling up, so prices stay fair for new players. The sell screen shows what you'll get after the tax.","Your character screen (the tab with your name): tap any slot with gear in it, or the name of the ring or amulet you're wearing, to see that item's card, with its stats, what a shop pays and its market price. The stats list now also shows health, armour, your block limit, critical hit chance, mana regen per second, every gear effect you're wearing (life steal, burn, bonus XP and so on), Turtle and Meteorite set pieces, and potion buffs with their time left.","Every item in your bag now shows what a shop pays for it next to its market price."]},
{v:'2026.11.16-25',d:'Nov 16, 2026',t:"Meteor strikes, Brewing, daggers, better maps and moderators",n:["Better maps: the minimap now follows you, zoomed in on the area around you, with an arrow showing which way you're facing. Your tracked quest shows on it as a gold dot, or a gold arrow on the edge when it's further away.","Map pins: tap anywhere on the map (HERE) to drop a pink pin. A pink arrow on screen shows the way and how far it is, and the pin is on your minimap too. Tap the pin on the map again to remove it, or just walk there. In a party, everyone sees each other's pins in green with the owner's name, on the map, the minimap and the ground.","Towns, dungeons, harbors, piers and the landmarks you've found are now named right on the map, so the colour key underneath is much shorter.","Guild quests can be tracked: find your guild's quest in the quest log (or tap Track in the quest tracker on the guild's Quest tab). The tracker shows the guild's progress while you gather anywhere.","Guild sails: fly your guild's colours on your boat. START > Style has a new Boat section: pick Guild sails and your sails take on your guild cape's design (colours, pattern, trim and emblem). The emblem is drawn large and outlined, centred on the sail above your head. Other players see them when you sail past.","Walking into a town no longer pops up a welcome message: every town is named on your map now.","Mithril and adamant arrows: fletch 15 mithril arrows from 1 mithril bar + 2 maple logs (Archery 40) or 15 adamant arrows from 1 adamant bar + 2 yew logs (Archery 55) in the Craft tab. Each step up hits 1 harder: iron arrows +1 over plain ones, mithril +2, adamant +3 and meteorite +4 (meteorite arrows got 1 stronger). Your bow always shoots the best arrows you carry first.","Vessa's potion stall in Emberwatch, the forge camp on Ashfall Coast: buy healing, strength, poison, swiftness, iron skin, napalm and electricity potions, and sell her the potions you brew for 1.5x what other shops pay.","Meteors also fall on Ashfall Coast, Briarwood Isle, Ironcrest Highlands and the Shattered Expanse now, not just Hollow. The banner tells everyone which island it's on, and a crater on an island flattens the trees and rocks where it lands until it's gone.","Meteor achievements (START > Achievements): help break a meteor core, break 10, do the most damage to one, break 25 meteorite veins, pick up 50 stardust, and help break one on an island.","The new deep-water fish (moonfin, abyssal eel and ancient koi) count toward summoning the Giant Turtle, and the guild bank's raw fish button puts them in too.","Guild fishing ponds: finishing the guild Fishing quest now lets the leader or an officer pick ponds as the reward (4 trout, 3 salmon, 2 swordfish, 1 moonfin or 1 koi pond; a mountain of bait is still an option). Dig one from the guild Bank tab while facing open ground on your guild island. Fish in it to catch that pond's fish much more often: moonfin at any time of day, and the ancient koi more than twice as often as in open water. Each pond has 30 catches for you, refilling one every 2 minutes, and everything you catch counts toward the next guild quest.","Only one player can fish a spot at a time now. If someone's line is already in that water, you'll see \"Someone is already fishing there.\" Step over a tile and cast again.","Better campfires: burn oak (Firemaking 15), willow (30), maple (45), yew (60) and void logs (75). Press F (the fire button) and pick which logs to use: 3 logs + 1 stone build a campfire that burns longer and gives much more XP, and each kind burns in its own colour, from bright willow flames to green yew and purple void fire. Standing next to one of your own fires, F also lets you feed it one log at a time to keep it going (up to 30 minutes) for XP, no stone needed.","New fish for high-level anglers: the moonfin (Fishing 70) only bites at night, the abyssal eel (Fishing 80) lives in the cold waters of the Shattered Expanse and Ironcrest, and the very rare ancient koi (Fishing 90) can bite anywhere. Cook them at Cooking 70, 80 and 90; they heal 6, 7 and 8 hearts.","Moderators: SkillQuest now has player moderators, trusted adult players who help keep chat safe. They can read public chat, private messages, party messages and guild chat, look into player reports, delete messages, and mute or suspend players who break the rules. Private messages are not private from moderators, so never share personal information (real name, address, school, phone number, passwords) in the game. The privacy policy (Options > ABOUT) explains what moderators can see.","Patrons can design pets in the Art Room: pick A pet and draw it facing right in four frames, Idle 1 and Idle 2 (it switches between them while it stands) and Walk 1 and Walk 2 (it steps between them as it follows you). The preview shows it standing or walking to and fro next to your character, at the size it will be in the game. Approved pets can be given to a pet in the game, with your name in the credits.","Fixed: on the Shattered Expanse you could keep getting hit (\"Ouch!\" every second) by something you couldn't see. A monster has to be on screen to touch you now, and the game sends a report when it stops one of these, so the cause can be tracked down.","Fixed: skeletons near another player could throw bones in a rapid stream. Monsters you see from another player's game now keep their own reload time, so skeletons throw at their normal pace again.","Fixed: meteors could come down one after another. Strikes are now at least 12 hours apart.","New skill: Brewing. Build a cauldron (Craft tab, Crafting 8: 10 stone, 2 iron bars, 4 wood), place it at home and press HIT to brew healing (Brewing 1), strength (10), poison (15), swiftness (20), iron skin (30), napalm (35) and electricity-in-a-bottle (55) potions from berries, mushrooms, bones, nuts and more. Its skill tree has perks at 20, 40, 60 and 80. While you brew, the cauldron boils and bubbles in the colour of the potion you're making.","Daggers are off-hand weapons now: iron and steel daggers from the anvil, plus new mithril (Attack 30), adamant (45), starsteel (60: 2 adamant bars + 4 stardust, Smithing 66) and meteorite (75) daggers. They add to your melee damage, give you a new ultimate, Potion Burst, and stab: press X or right-click (R1 on a controller, the STAB button on touch screens) for a quick dagger jab. Stabs are weaker than sword swings but come faster and fit in between them, so sword plus dagger fight together. Other players see your dagger jab too.","Potion Burst: pin any potion in your bag (select it, tap ☆ DAGGER ULT) and pick Potion Burst in the equipment screen. ULT then uses that potion: a healing or buff potion is drunk by you AND by party members and friends standing near you (it only uses one of yours). Poison, napalm and electricity coat your dagger for 20 seconds instead: poison poisons every monster you hit, napalm sets every one on fire, and electricity sends lightning to up to two more monsters nearby. 20 second cooldown, no mana. You can also coat your dagger by using those potions from the bag.","Burning monsters now show proper flames.","Fixed: Shattered Expanse sharks bit players standing on the beach, hidden behind them. Sharks still circle close to the shore when you're hurt, but they only bite on the water (in your boat), and a biting shark now shows over you.","Fixed: stabbing with a Stone Sledgehammer in your main hand showed the hammer swinging instead of the dagger.","Fixed: chests, the bag and other screens with iron or steel daggers in them stopped opening after the Brewing update (another screen showed instead). Nothing was lost: your items were there all along.","Meteor strikes: about once a day (never twice within 12 hours) a meteor falls somewhere wild on Hollow Island or one of the four big islands (never near a village or anyone's home). Everyone online gets a warning a minute before, sees it streak across the sky, and a banner and map marker show where it landed. Anyone with a pickaxe can mine the glowing core, and the three players who do the most damage get 750, 500 or 300 of the best ore their Mining level can mine plus a tenth of that in meteorite ore (everyone else who helps gets 100 + 10). The meteorite veins around it need Mining 70 and a steel pickaxe or better, take about 40 hits each and give 1-3 meteorite ore. Pick up stardust from the sparkles on the rim. The crater cools after 15 minutes.","Meteorite gear, forged at an anvil from meteorite bars (smelt 15 meteorite ore, 15 adamant ore and 3 stardust at a furnace, Smithing 80). Everything needs level 75 in its skill: meteorite helmet, chestplate and legs (Defence 75; more block than adamant, and a set bonus for wearing all three), pickaxe and axe (Mining / Woodcutting 75; the fastest tools there are), bow (Archery 75; the hardest-hitting, furthest-shooting bow) and wand (Magic 75). The meteorite wand shoots mini meteorites that splash nearby monsters, and its ultimate, METEOR FALL, calls a meteor down on your foes for a big explosion. Meteorite arrows (25 from 1 bar + 2 void logs in the Craft tab, Archery 75) are the hardest-hitting arrows there are.","The Mining and Woodcutting skill trees now show every tree and ore you unlock (oak, willow, maple and yew trees; gold, mithril and adamant veins and boulders; meteor cores and meteorite veins) and which tool you need.","Skill trees now list every piece of gear and every recipe at the level it needs: what you can wear or use at each Defence, Attack, Magic, Archery, Woodcutting or Mining level, and what you can smith, craft or cook at each level. New gear added to the game shows up there by itself.","Stuck? Type /stuck in chat. It takes you out of any room, back to the pier on an island, or to the Tidewatch harbor post on Hollow (once every 2 minutes, not during duels or boss fights).","Fixed: sailing home from an island (including your guild island) could drop you in the sea when the trip was started from inside a house, yard or dungeon, for example with the guild horn. You now always land on solid ground, and old saves with a bad landing spot are put right when you sail home.","Graves are now locked to their owner for the first 5 minutes, so you have time to get back to your things. After that, anyone can take what's left, as before.","Fixed: the cauldron now uses the chests in your house or castle like the furnace, anvil and stove do. Ingredients come from your bag first, then your chests.","Fixed: the Mining perks that keep a rock standing now work on gold, mithril and adamant veins, rocks in dungeons and boulders too.","Fixed: sailing to Hollow could put you back on the island you had just come from (for example your guild island).","Fixed: lots of campfires close together made the game lag at night. Fires side by side now share one glow."]},
 {v:'2026.11.15-22',d:'Nov 15, 2026',t:"Patrons, safer chat, pets at home, combat rebalance",n:["Patrons: support SkillQuest on Patreon (START > Patron) and get a flame next to your name, an animated fire cape that's yours to keep, your name in the new Credits, and the Art Room, where you can draw sprites and animations and send them in to be added to the game. Perks are cosmetic only. Ask a parent first if you're under 18.","The Patron Art Gallery opened in Hollow Village (north of the World Market). Every painting in it was drawn by a SkillQuest Patron, and Iris sells prints. Hang a painting at home: face a wall and PLACE to hang it, or place it on the floor to stand it on an easel. Face any painting to see who painted it.","Patrons can draw things to wear in the Art Room (Something to wear): hats, tops and trousers drawn right on your character from the front, back and side. The best ones can become real gear.","Everything for Patrons is on one screen: START > Patron shows your perks, opens the Art Room and the fire cape, and has the Patreon buttons. Join with the email you sign in with and your perks switch on by themselves.","Every cape in one place: START > Style now lists your Marlo capes, your guild cape and the fire cape, with a picture of how you look from the back and the front. The one you're wearing has a check mark.","The Art Room is rebuilt for phones: the tools sit in a row above the canvas, the colours right under it, zoom in and move around (two fingers or the move tool), a mirror mode that draws both sides at once, and a separate page for naming and sending. On a computer: B/E/G/I for the tools, M for mirror, Ctrl+Z to undo.","New Credits screen in Options > About.","Safer for younger players: the game asks for your birth year once (only your age group is kept). Players under 13 chat with ready-made phrases, can only trade, message and duel with friends, and never show their real name.","New PHRASES button in the chat box: tap to send a quick line like \"Want to team up?\" or \"Good game!\".","Chat filter: swear words, slurs, email addresses, phone numbers and outside links are starred out. Character and chest names are checked too.","Terms of Service, Privacy Policy and Refund Policy pages, linked from the title screen and Options > About.","Options > Delete my account removes your character and data for good.","Show off your pets: pick a pet in your bag and tap PLACE while you're in your house, castle, backyard or courtyard. They live there now: they roam around, stop to look about, nap (more at night), play chase with each other, get the zoomies, and trot over to greet you or any friend who visits, then tag along for a bit. HIT a pet to give it a pat (visitors can too); HIT it again within 3 seconds to pick it back up.","Chests: TAKE ALL moves everything into your bag, and SORT orders the chest by type, name, amount or value (it remembers your choice). Tap ✎ RENAME to give a chest a name of up to 12 letters. The name shows on the chest screen and on a little placard on the front of the chest, which visitors see too.","Magic: every spell costs 1 mana less (fire and ice 1, storm and void 2), mana comes back 3 times as fast, and every spell does 1 more damage. Wands now keep up through a long fight instead of running dry after a few casts.","Archery: every arrow does 1 more damage, so early bows keep up with early swords.","Together with yesterday's slower sword hits (one every 0.4 seconds), melee, bows and wands now deal about the same damage over a fight. Melee still hits everything in front of you, bows and wands hit from a distance, and spells can burn, freeze or shock.","Rain now waters the crops in your backyard and courtyard too.","Jewelry at the furnace uses the gold bars and gems in your house's chests, like smelting does.","Campfire cooking keeps going while you open your skills, bag or other menus.","Rings and amulets can be put on (or swapped) right from the equipment screen: the Ring and Amulet slots list the jewelry in your bag.","Online play uses much less data: your game now sends only what changed about you and the monsters around you, instead of everything several times a second. Easier on phone data plans, and it keeps the game's servers running smoothly as more players join.","Fixed: chest names on castle chests disappeared after every update.","Fixed: beds couldn't be picked up with the USE button. Tap a bed once (you'll wake up there), then HIT or USE it again within 3 seconds: both buttons say PICK UP.","Fixed: when a campfire burned out mid-cooking you started eating the food raw; cooking now stops. Tapping COOK again while cooking no longer restarts it with the first recipe in the list.","Fixed: the CHAT and BUG buttons covered the map and other screens on phones.","Fixed: HIT next to a tree or rock could shoot at a nearby monster instead of chopping or mining (touch and controller).","Fixed: the seed cursor in backyards showed red on tilled soil.","Fixed: world bosses stayed on the map after being defeated.","Fixed: Saltmere's moored boats sat on the grass north of town.","Fixed: some berry bushes, rocks and trees on the islands couldn't be reached (cut off by water or cliffs); they're gone.","Fixed: START > PvP opened the Custom Controls screen instead, so PvP couldn't be turned off. It opens the PvP screen again (Custom Controls is still under Options > Controls).","Fixed: chest names on homes on the islands (and guild islands) didn't show for visitors. They do now; the owner just needs to be on this update.","Fixed: while you visit a friend's backyard or courtyard, chests they rename (and furniture or crops they change) now show up within a few seconds instead of only after you walk out and back in.","Fixed: furniture and chests could be placed in backyard and courtyard ponds.","Fixed: arrows and spells stopped at the water's edge on the islands. They now fly over water everywhere, and you can shoot and cast from your boat while sailing around an island (the arrow used to vanish).","Fixed: other players couldn't see you shoot your bow, and your arrows couldn't hit players in duels or PvP. Everyone nearby sees your arrows again.","Fixed: campfires on the islands burned out twice as fast as they should (a Lone Bonfire lasted about 15 minutes instead of 30). They now last their full time everywhere.","Fixed: some foods and items added in updates (like pizza) had no description in the bag. They now show what they heal and fill, and a short line about them.","Fixed: tapping Become a Patron in Options could trip an error in the background.","Fixed: the Patron Art Gallery was squeezed in right behind a player's house. It now never sits on or against a player's house.","Fixed: on a computer, the Art Room's colours and frames ran off the right edge of the window."]},
 {v:'2026.11.14-47',d:'Nov 14, 2026',t:"Guilds, guild bosses and capes",n:["Guilds: found one from START > Guild for 5,000,000 gold with a name, a 2-4 letter tag and a colour. Your tag shows over your head. Leaders and officers invite players by walking up to them and choosing INVITE TO GUILD. Leaders can change the tag for free, and rename the guild (the first rename is free, then 1,000,000 gold).","Guild islands: every guild gets its own island, sailed to from any harbor post, with a guild board, a bank chest and your banner. Leaders and officers plant saplings, ore veins and bushes there, every member can gather them, and they grow back in a minute.","Guild Quests: huge goals the whole guild works on together, like cutting 100,000 trees or catching 50,000 fish. Everything members gather anywhere counts. A finished quest pays a reward into the guild bank (saplings up to Void saplings, ore veins, bushes, seeds, spores or bait) and ranks the guild up in that skill.","Guild skill ranks (up to 5): each rank gives every member +10% XP and a 10% chance of an extra item when gathering with that skill, anywhere in the world.","Guild buildings arrive as the guild levels up: the Guild horn at level 2 (travel to the island from anywhere outdoors), the Guild forge at level 3 (furnace and anvil, +20% Smithing XP), the Guild shrine at level 4 (a daily 20-minute blessing) and the Guild hall at level 5 (+10 members and +5% XP in every skill).","Guild bank: a chest for everyone, with a daily withdrawal limit per rank set by the leader and a log of every deposit and withdrawal. Buttons put in all your void logs, raw fish, logs or ores at once, or everything in your bag (tap twice).","Guild chat (the Guild tab in chat, or type /g) and Top guilds (START > Guild > Top guilds).","Guild bosses, once a week each, from START > Guild > Bosses. The Void Treant costs 50,000 void logs and 1 Woodcutting rank; everyone who fights it gets a Void wand every time, the strongest wand in the game (Magic 50, every fourth hit heals you, ultimate: Void Rift). Your axe and Woodcutting level add damage to every melee hit on it.","The Giant Turtle costs 5,000 raw fish (any kinds, cheapest first) and 1 Fishing rank. Dive into the whirlpool by your guild's pier together; everyone gets a Turt fragment every time. Smith Turtle armor from the fragments at an anvil: helm (1), legs (2) and chestplate (2). It's the best armor in the game (Defence 50), and each piece you wear raises your block chance. Your Fishing level and rod add damage to every melee hit on it.","Void trees (on the Shattered Expanse, and void saplings on guild islands) now give void logs, for summoning the Void Treant.","Guild capes: wear yours from START > Guild > Members. The leader designs it in Settings: two colours, a pattern, a trim and one of 13 emblems (including Tree, Fish and Skull) in any colour.","Capes look like real cloth now, guild capes and Marlo's capes alike: they roll over your shoulders and fall in folds to a wavy hem, clasp at your collar, and swing and billow as you walk. They go over robes and armour, while hoods and hats sit on top.","Smarter eating: EAT picks the smallest food that heals what's missing and saves your good food when you're healthy. Select a food in your Bag and tap ☆ EAT FIRST to make it your favourite. Cooking at a campfire with several kinds of raw food asks what to cook.","Chat shows as speech bubbles over players' heads, kept clear of your buttons and map. Options > Chat: HIDDEN removes the bubbles and the CHAT button (chat is still in the START menu).","Leaderboards are in the START menu. Phones held sideways show the START menu in three columns so everything fits.","Voyages all come from Sera, the Navigator in Tidewatch: she gives out every voyage, takes your reports, fits boat upgrades and shows what's coming next. Harbor posts are fast travel to the islands you've charted.","The Wiki has a Home page with your next steps, voyages with your own progress, how to reach each island, and the latest patch notes first.","Punchier fights: sparks when you strike, a puff of smoke when a monster falls, and a little screen shake on big hits (turn it off in Options > Screen shake).","Critical hits from gear and perks now deal 1.5x to 2x damage, shown as one big pink number. Before, a crit just repeated the hit for the same damage.","Melee balance: sword hits on monsters now come at most every 0.4 seconds, however fast you tap or hold the button (holding R2 or Space used to swing much faster). Chopping, mining and fishing are as fast as before.","You can talk to villagers while they sleep: stand by their bed and tap TALK. Night quests (like Corin in Tidewatch) work again.","Emotes have new animations: a real wave, a deeper bow, dancing, a jumping cheer, a shaking laugh, a beating heart, yes and no signs, a thinking bubble, and sleeping lying down.","Redrawn trousers and leg armour step with your legs as you walk.","Smith all, Smelt all, Make all and the new All button for rings and amulets show how many are left over your head.","Recipe lists show every material by its name.","Backyards and courtyards: rain and snow fall there, bows, wands and ultimates work (train Archery and Magic on a dummy), and friends visiting see your campfires and can cook at them.","Tidier phone screen: the getting-started hint sits under your quest box, the ONLINE and BUG buttons are smaller and side by side, short messages no longer pile onto your XP numbers, the minimap no longer hides under HIT when sideways, and there's one TALK button instead of two.","Backups: your game is still backed up every day. If you ever lose progress, use Report a bug and we'll restore it for you.","Island and guild bosses: once a boss falls, everyone in its lair is walked back outside after a few seconds. To fight it again, open the door with a new set of sigil shards (or summon a guild boss again next week).","The Wiki has a Guilds page: founding and joining, the guild island, quests, levels and ranks, buildings, the bank, both guild bosses, Turtle armor and capes.","New things can now arrive with the islands: quests with several steps and reward choices, scheduled events (a green pill at the top shows what's on), hand-made dungeons, new crops, new places on Hollow and pets with powers.","Fixed: a Bone bow turned into a Longbow every time you loaded the game. Your Bone bow is back.","Fixed: void logs didn't show in your bag, and castles, paintings, clocks and some other items were listed twice.","Fixed: a house or castle on your guild island could disappear when you played on another device. A home on the island of a guild you've left goes back into your bag.","Fixed: monsters knocked into a wall became impossible to hit, and the imp kept attacking after an island boss was beaten.","Fixed: playing only with a controller could leave the game silent.","Fixed: anvils, furnaces and other station screens looked squashed, the controller highlight floated over windows, and party health bars hid behind the CHAT and BUG buttons.","Fixed: a guild could go over its member limit when several invites were accepted at once. A full guild now says so when you try to join.","Fixed: critical hit, burn, slow and life steal perks only worked while you were also wearing gear with a special effect."]},
 {v:'2026.11.13-38',d:'Nov 13, 2026',t:"One save on your account, new music and PvP rebalance",n:["Sign in with Google to play. Your character lives in your Google account, the same on phone, computer and the Windows app. Only one device can play at a time: the other one stops with a PLAY HERE INSTEAD button. If your connection drops you'll see \"Not saved: reconnecting...\".","A brand-new orchestral soundtrack: 18 original songs, a theme for every island, a sailing song and boss music.","PvP rebalance: your gear and levels count against players (hits do 1 to 3 hearts), heavy armour softens big hits, blocking stops at most 1 in 4 player attacks, healing is halved while fighting a player, and duels turn to SUDDEN DEATH after a minute.","Bigger, prettier backyards and courtyards, set in a forest clearing with ponds, paths and trees. Chop the trees, pick the bushes and fish in the pond; they grow back after a few minutes. Light campfires there too.","No more getting hungry at home: food doesn't go down inside your house or castle. Wardrobes can be picked up.","Build at home: fences, walls, chests, beds, stations and furniture now go inside your house or castle, or in its yard. Anything you had built outside was packed into your bag.","Controllers reach everything: trade, party and duel requests, every menu, text boxes (with a new on-screen keyboard) and item cards, with a bright gold ring around what you've selected.","HIT no longer tills or waters: use X or right-click on a computer, R1 on a controller, or the new TILL / WATER button on touch screens.","Chests have a DEPOSIT BAG button.","Farming: more seeds as you level up, and three new Farming perks (Seed Pouch, Twin Seeds and Heirloom Seeds).","Pick your ultimate: if your gear gives more than one, choose which in the Gear tab.","Stove meals made from several ingredients, and food that gives buffs: Wisdom (+20% XP) and Regeneration.","New gear effects: more melee, arrow or magic damage, faster mana and health regeneration, slower hunger and more gold from monsters.","Arrows, bows and ranger gear take time to make, with an All button.","World Market: no maximum price any more.","Report players: tap someone's name and choose REPORT. Rule breakers can be muted or suspended. Ignored someone by mistake? Choose UNIGNORE, or find them under IGNORED in Chat > Friends.","Gifts and replies from the developer arrive in your game, announcements show as a banner, and XP events show a purple tag with the time left.","New content now arrives while you play, without reloading.","Phones stay awake while you play.","Fixed: a Warlord's blade, mithril or adamant axe or pickaxe turned into steel when you loaded the game. Lost ones were put back in your bag.","Fixed: logging in could put you back at the spawn point.","Fixed: furniture by a back door could trap you, and anything packed up on an island could come back.","Fixed: the Safe Haven and Sacred Flames perks did nothing, and the Mushling and Glowcap left the PET slot looking empty.","Fixed: burrowing beetles never came back out of the sand.","Fixed: you couldn't place a castle after packing up your house while other houses were nearby.","Fixed: music stuttered in the background, gifts got stuck, emote commands in chat posted the word, and new gear looks showed as the item they were based on.","Fixed: \"undefined\" in the general store and crafting screen, and world bosses appearing where you couldn't reach them."]},
 {v:'2026.11.12-20',d:'Nov 12, 2026',t:"Chapter two, duels, chess, parties and backyards",n:["Elder Rowan's story goes on: chapter two sends you across the sea to Briarwood, Thornbrook, the Ashfall Coast and an island boss, ending with Legend of the Isles (beat all five island bosses for 5,000 gold). The quest box tells you which voyage or boat upgrade you need next.","Backyards and courtyards: every house has a back door to a private yard, and castles open onto a grand courtyard. Place furniture and farm there; only trusted friends can visit. Castle halls are symmetrical, with a new throne.","One home each: one house or castle in the world. Extra ones were packed into your bag with everything inside.","Achievements and a collection log: START > Achievements, over 40 goals that pay gold.","Walk up to another player and tap their name for TRADE, ADD FRIEND, INVITE TO PARTY, DUEL or CHESS.","Duels with stakes of items and gold: the winner takes both stakes. Duel wins count as PvP kills on the leaderboard.","Chess against other players, with stakes and a rating ladder (Leaderboards > Chess). Grandmaster Orla is easier to beat, and Opening Moves is her own side quest.","Parties of up to 4: +10% XP when together, a Party chat tab, a share of each other's gold, and a star over each member.","Emotes acted out by your character: START > Emotes, G on a keyboard, or /wave, /dance, /sit and more in chat.","Weekly events: the whole server works toward one goal, and everyone who helped gets gold and XP.","Change your keys and controller buttons in Options > Controls, and move or resize the touch buttons on phones.","Options > Check for updates, and an \"Update ready\" bar when a new version is out.","Smooth camera: no more shaky screen while walking.","Your weapon is drawn with its own item picture when you swing, chop, mine, cast and shoot. HIT no longer casts spells: use CAST.","The hoe and watering can are off-hand items: X or right-click uses your off-hand, and farming swaps between them for you.","Smith iron, steel, mithril and adamant axes and pickaxes at the anvil, and craft a fishing rod.","Skill perks that do what they say: Flame Aura makes you glow, speed perks really speed things up, and the Golden perks cover everything they should.","Fall in a dungeon or boss lair and your grave appears just outside the entrance.","World bosses show on the map and minimap, and a count of players online sits above the day box.","Far fewer pop-ups: short messages float over your head, and on upright phones the message box sits at the top.","Your houses show on the map, Hollow Island has open sea all the way round, and there's a JOIN OUR DISCORD button on the title screen.","Fixed: Slime quests count slimes only, Night Watch means a whole night, and repeated quest tasks were replaced.","Fixed: the TALK button flickering, cooking on castles, boats riding onto bridges, item stats showing twice, and quest names like \"Defeat the Dunes\"."]},
 {v:'2026.11.11-14',d:'Nov 11, 2026',t:"Island bosses together, a friendlier start and daily challenges",n:["Fight island bosses together: open the door while a friend is inside and you join their fight. The boss switches targets and gets tougher for each fighter, and everyone gets the full reward.","A Getting started guide for new players, with glowing buttons, hints and small rewards.","Daily challenges: three small tasks a day at the top of your quest log, paying gold and XP, with a streak bonus.","Item cards in chests: see an item's details and choose how many to move.","Smithing, smelting and crafting are acted out by your character, and others see it.","Pets that help: treelings give extra logs, and two new mushroom pets, the Mushling (heals you) and the Glowcap (slows monsters that hit you).","Buttons say what they do: CHOP, MINE, PICK, FISH, SMELT, OPEN, SLEEP, READ and more.","A fairer World Market: up to 2 offers per item, a minimum price, a warning before a price far from the usual, and offers last 7 days.","Quest tracking shows the next village step in Three Villages, One Island, and you can stop tracking quests.","On phones and tablets, chat opens at the bottom and moves above the keyboard.","New islands can have people to talk to, their own dungeons and monster areas."]},
 {v:'2026.11.10-4',d:'Nov 10, 2026',t:"Skilling you can see",n:["Fishing, lighting fires and cooking are acted out by your character instead of a progress bar, and other players see it too.","The Stone Sledgehammer breaks any rock or ore in one hit, GROUND SLAM smashes everything you could mine around you, and others see the shockwave.","Fixed: the online count showed players who had already left."]},
 {v:'2026.11.09-10',d:'Nov 9, 2026',t:"Skilling takes time and tougher bosses",n:["Cooking, firemaking, smelting, smithing, crafting and reeling in fish take a few seconds each. Make all and Cook all keep going until you run out.","All bosses are much tougher, and you can only eat once every 3 seconds.","Shops keep a daily stock that restocks every morning.","Item names show under every bag, chest and bank slot.","Sigil shards drop twice as often.","New: skill tomes. Read one for XP in its skill.","New gear, gear looks, gear effects (life steal, burning, slowing, critical hits, faster walking, bonus XP) and new islands with treasure chests can now arrive without a full update.","Fixed: World Market trades always failing, cooking at a stove doing nothing, and stations not using materials from nearby chests.","Fixed: other players didn't see redesigned gear, regrown trees on tilled soil couldn't be chopped, and the Options screen sometimes wouldn't open."]},
 {v:'2026.11.07-2',d:'Nov 7, 2026',t:"Safer saves across devices",n:["Fixed a serious bug that could overwrite newer progress when you played on more than one device.","Your save is backed up to your account every day you play and whenever it's replaced."]},
 {v:'2026.11.06-16',d:'Nov 6, 2026',t:"Island bosses, a new quest log and the Windows app",n:["Island bosses: the sealed doors on every island now open with five sigil shards. Inside wait the Briar Queen, the Iron Warlord, the Frost Wyrm, the Void Herald and Black Jack, the Outlaw King, each with animated attacks, wind-ups to watch for and a 5% rare drop.","A new quest log (Q) with Active, Available and Done tabs. Track a quest to get its next step in the quest box and a golden arrow pointing the way.","Pets are items: a new PET slot on the equipment screen, and every other pet you own is in your bag.","Climb the plateaus on Ironcrest, No Man's Land and Ashfall by the stairways cut into the cliffs.","SkillQuest for Windows: its own app with the same accounts and saves.","Options shows your Google account, with Sign out and Switch Google account.","Tap the minimap to open the full map. The menu is now two columns.","Fixed: Google sign-in on phones and tablets, getting stuck sailing between islands, a slow world map, and stairways you couldn't climb."]},
 {v:'2026.11.05-24',d:'Nov 5, 2026',t:"The islands update",n:["New rare drops: an Imp pet (Demon), the Flame Crown (Flame Wisp), a Castle (Stone Giant) and the Stone Sledgehammer with its GROUND SLAM ultimate (Stone Giant).","Briarwood's village Thornbrook and Ashfall's forge camp Emberwatch, each with quests, a shop and buildings to walk into.","New dungeons: Thornroot Hollow (with the Thornheart) and Cinderdeep (with the Emberlord), plus deeper mines and caves on Ironcrest.","New island: No Man's Land, a lawless desert where PvP is always on, reached by the Lawless Waters voyage.","The World Market just outside Hollow Village: buy and sell anything with every player.","Hollow Island is twice as big, and your builds moved with it.","Farming and fishing on every island, each island with its own fish, and you can sail off the edge of the map between islands.","Brand-new sailboats, and the sea now stretches past the edge of the map.","More Foraging (mushrooms and hazelnuts), boulders to break, and rare pets: wolves, treelings, the Squirrel and ore golems.","See your sword when you swing it.","Craft a hoe and watering can, and throw things away in a Trash can.","Your grave shows on the map and minimap, with an arrow pointing to it.","The Wiki: skills, items, crafting, monsters, bosses, dungeons, quests, islands, pets, guides and maps, with search. Patch notes are in it too.","Calmer monsters, gates that keep monsters out, a pier trader on every island, and a new app icon.","Fixed: landing your boat with a controller, getting stuck in regrown trees, and the flame wisp appearing far from your campfire."]},
 {v:'2026.11.04-4',d:'Nov 4, 2026',t:"World bosses",n:["World bosses: the Flame Wisp, Stone Giant, Demon and Ancient Dragon appear every 30 minutes. Fight them together and earn loot by damage rank. The Ancient Dragon can drop the Dragonsoul Amulet (Dragon Form).","Houses on any island, leaderboards, sailing around the islands, Firemaking perks, and mithril and adamant bows and wands.","Trusted friends can use your stations, chests and beds. Ignore and report players from chat.","A Fullscreen button, a Hide helmet option and the game version in Options.","Opening the game on a second device or tab pauses the older one.","Fixed: names turning into \"Adventurer\", monsters standing on top of you, and invisible campfires on other islands."]},
 {v:'2026.11.03',d:'Nov 3, 2026',t:'Playing together',n:['Trading, public gravestones (your items wait 15 minutes where you fell), and opt-in PvP with safe zones.','See other players\' swings, arrows, spells and ultimates.','Build and cook on every island. Gold jewelry with gems. Marlo\'s Emporium: pets, capes, dyes, fine furniture and potions.','A shared world: one clock, shared trees, rocks, monsters, dungeons and campfires. Friends, private messages and friend requests.','Visit friends\' houses; see each other\'s farms, builds and boats.','A title screen, controller support, mouse and touch aiming, and a bug report button.']},
 {v:'2026.11.02',d:'Nov 2, 2026',t:'Online!',n:['SkillQuest goes online: Google sign-in, saves on your account, other players and chat.','OG crowns for everyone who signs in before Dec 3, 2026.']}];
window.SQVER=PATCH_NOTES[0].v;
